TA-journald
====

Collects journald log-plane metadata: journal disk usage (journalctl --disk-usage), journal file count under /var/log/journal, total journal size, age of the oldest journal file, and the journald service state. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype journald:status) and journald.* metrics (disk_kb, size_mb, file_count) to index=metrics (sourcetype journald:metrics) every 300s, with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * systemd-journald (standard on systemd hosts)
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="journald:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="journald:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="journald.*" by host
  | mstats avg("journald.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=journald:status  (disk_kb, size_mb, file_count, oldest_age_hours, service state)
Metrics: journald.disk_kb, journald.size_mb, journald.file_count on index=metrics
Alarm status when journal disk usage exceeds 8 GB.
Dashboards: TA-Journald > Journald Overview / Journald Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-journald/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * disk-usage parsing tolerates the '4.2G' style; falls back to a filesystem walk of /var/log/journal.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-journald).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-journald/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
